From: Stefano Viola <stefano.viola@toradex.com>
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: optionally exit when the USB connection closes

On Android, init rebinds the USB gadget when adbd reopens FunctionFS
(sys.usb.ffs.ready). Elsewhere nothing does, so after a cable replug the
host sees adbd as offline until a reboot. With ADBD_EXIT_ON_USB_DISCONNECT
set, exit instead and let the service manager set the gadget up again.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Stefano Viola <stefano.viola@toradex.com>
---
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/usb.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/usb.cpp
@@ -343,6 +343,14 @@
 
                         enabled = false;
                         running = false;
+
+                        // Without Android init nobody rebinds the gadget once FunctionFS is
+                        // reopened (and tearing the connection down can block): exit and let
+                        // the service manager set the gadget up again.
+                        if (getenv("ADBD_EXIT_ON_USB_DISCONNECT")) {
+                            LOG(INFO) << "USB function disabled, exiting";
+                            exit(0);
+                        }
                         break;
 
                     case FUNCTIONFS_UNBIND:
